 //   Touch-down ownership (dm_pad_menu_takes and dm_pad_hit in DmPadGeometry.h): the menu button where it is nearer than a locked key (a view of its own, DmMenuButton), locked keys next (shoulders, − / +, L3 / R3), the jump and photo buttons next, then whichever of the diamond and the left stick has the smallest distance / grab radius (the left half holds the floating stick),
 //     then in 3D the right stick for a touch in the right third. X, ZR, R, L3, R3 and the D-pad are hidden and disabled: a touch on one of them falls through to the floating stick (left half) or the right stick (right third) instead.
 //   The player can move single controls in the shell's settings (DM_TOUCH_LAYOUT, one arrangement per layout): the geometry places each only where it fits and keeps the rest where they were.
-//   The in-game menu's "按键设置" (button settings) opens a panel above the game: tapping an icon selects it, a slider for the selected icon's own size and dragging the icons to move them, saved per icon in NSUserDefaults (DmPadLineLayout) so it survives a restart; and a slider for the glass effect's strength (0-100%, the game's own setting, NSUserDefaults DmPadGlassOpacity): 70% is the look as shipped, 100% is the deepest the glass gets.
+//   The in-game menu's "按键设置" (button settings) opens a panel above the game: tapping an icon selects it, a slider for the selected icon's own size and dragging the icons to move them, saved per icon in NSUserDefaults (DmPadLineLayout) so it survives a restart; and a slider for the glass effect's strength (0-100%, the game's own setting, NSUserDefaults DmPadGlassOpacity): 70% is the look as shipped, 100% is the deepest the glass gets. 0146: an eye toggle in the panel hides / shows the selected icon (hidden icons are not drawn and cannot be pressed; the menu gear is never hideable, so the eye is disabled for it); while the panel is open a hidden icon is shown dimmed, so it can be tapped to unhide it.
 //   Everything hugs the edges and corners to leave the picture room; each control is one
 //   image layer (dm/ios/Sources/PadIcons/pad_line_*.png, the line set, bundled as resources):
 //   the artwork never changes on press (no pressed state), only the left stick's knob moves,
